= The Names They Took Down

Local councillors ask whether Lewica will merely oppose new removals or restore
names already taken down. Edward Gierek is the test case: authoritarian rule
and debt, but also housing, industry and a memory not reducible to an IPN file.

Socialist line: **[+ hard_left_line_label +]**. KO relation: **[+ ko_relation
+]/100**. Lewica polling: **[+ left_poll +]%**. Acceptance of capitalism:
**[+ capitalism_acceptance +]/100**.

- @decommunisation_repeal
- @decommunisation_unlawful
- @decommunisation_review
- @decommunisation_refuse

@decommunisation_repeal
title: Repeal the act and permit a democratic Gierek rehabilitation
subtitle: Use statute, hearings and local votes. The socialist current gains; the liberal centre recoils.
on-arrival: hard_left_line += 10; gierek_rehabilitation = 1; pzpr_history_concessions -= 1; razem_strength += 2; pps_strength += 2; progressives_strength += 1; razem_dissent -= 7; progressives_dissent -= 5; pps_dissent -= 6; razem_cooperation += 5; workers_support += 3; anti_establishment_youth_left_affinity += 3; left_economic_position -= 3; capitalism_acceptance -= 5; ko_relation -= 7; p2050_relation -= 5; psl_relation -= 4; left_poll -= 0.5; public_trust -= 2; barons_dissent -= 2; spring_dissent += 5; market_liberal_support += 5; constitutional_restraint += 2; news_headline = "Lewica proposes repeal of decommunisation and local restoration votes"

The bill ends administrative naming orders and returns decisions to elected
councils after public hearings. It makes room to restore Gierek without asking
anyone to rehabilitate censorship or the party-state with him.

- #poland_card_finish

@decommunisation_unlawful
title: Unlawful: tell Lewica councils to defy the IPN orders now
subtitle: Pursue municipal restoration before repeal, despite the statute. Legal exposure and dualism rise sharply.
on-arrival: hard_left_line += 13; hard_left_exposure += 17; gierek_rehabilitation = 1; pzpr_history_concessions -= 2; razem_strength += 3; pps_strength += 2; razem_dissent -= 10; progressives_dissent -= 7; pps_dissent -= 7; razem_cooperation += 7; anti_establishment_youth_left_affinity += 5; anti_system_trust += 4; capitalism_acceptance -= 7; ko_relation -= 10; p2050_relation -= 7; psl_relation -= 6; left_poll -= 0.9; public_trust -= 4; constitutional_restraint -= 9; government_procedural_restraint -= 7; judicial_legitimacy -= 6; legal_dualism += 10; market_liberal_support += 8; news_headline = "Lewica councils openly defy decommunisation orders"

The instruction is explicit: restore the names, refuse the substitute signs
and litigate only after the fact. It may create the political confrontation
needed for repeal. It is also an instruction to break a law still in force.

- #poland_card_finish

@decommunisation_review
title: Review only the least defensible removals
subtitle: A case-by-case commission preserves legality and avoids a general reversal. The current remains dissatisfied.
on-arrival: hard_left_line += 2; institutional_trust += 2; constitutional_restraint += 2; public_trust += 1; ko_relation += 1; p2050_relation += 1; pzpr_history_concessions += 1; razem_dissent += 4; progressives_dissent += 3; pps_dissent += 4; razem_cooperation -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica asks a commission to review decommunisation case by case"

The commission may save a few trade unionists, teachers and local organisers
from the same category as security officials. It cannot answer why the IPN
should retain the final word over an elected council.

- #poland_card_finish

@decommunisation_refuse
title: Refuse any reversal of decommunisation
subtitle: Free. Preserve the centrist firewall; repeated refusals compound left-current dissent.
on-arrival: {!
const refusalAnger = 1 + 0.6 * Math.max(0, Number(Q.hard_left_refusals) || 0);
Q.hard_left_refusals += 1;
Q.poland_decommunisation_timer = 7;
Q.razem_dissent += Math.round(6 * refusalAnger);
Q.progressives_dissent += Math.round(4 * refusalAnger);
Q.pps_dissent += Math.round(6 * refusalAnger);
Q.razem_cooperation -= Math.round(3 * refusalAnger);
Q.internal_dissent += Math.round(2 * refusalAnger);
Q.news_headline = "Lewica refuses to reverse decommunisation";
!}

The leadership says no democratic socialist needs Gierek Street. PPS asks why
the same leadership lets the national-conservative state decide who counts as
a democratic socialist.

- #poland_card_finish


@internationale
title: The Internationale
subtitle: Decide whether socialist language belongs on Lewica's stage or only in its archive.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
